# Async Patterns

Canon applies: `Promise.all` / `allSettled` semantics (MDN), the Node.js "Don't Block the Event Loop" guide, `@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises`. This rule holds only this project's decisions.

## Rules

1. **Independent awaits run in parallel.** If B does not depend on A, use `Promise.all`; use `Promise.allSettled` when some results are optional, and handle each rejection.
2. **Every external call has a timeout**, set with `AbortSignal.timeout(ms)`. Defaults: internal service 3s, external API 10s, long-running work 60s with progress events; database queries at the connection-pool level.
3. **Bound fan-out.** Mapping a large collection to promises uses a concurrency limit; default 10.
4. **Do not block the event loop.** `JSON.parse` / `JSON.stringify` of a payload over 1MB, sync file reads in hot paths and CPU-heavy loops go to a stream, `fs.promises` or a worker thread.
5. **Rejections** are handled per `error-handling.mdc` Rule 4.

---

## Review severities (shared with reviewers)

`review-logic` rates these patterns by this table. Change a row here, never in a reviewer.

| Signal | A finding when | Default | Not a finding |
|---|---|---|---|
| Sequential independent awaits (Rule 1) | always | `minor`; `major` on a hot path or when the calls are many | an ordering the code depends on |
| `Promise.all` where an optional result's failure discards a required one (Rule 1) | a named optional call can reject | `major` | all results required |
| External call with no timeout (Rule 2) | the call can hang a request or worker | `major` | a timeout set at the client or pool |
| Timeout built from `AbortController` + `setTimeout` (Rule 2) | always | `minor` | — |
| Unbounded fan-out over a caller-sized collection (Rule 3) | the size is not fixed small | `major` on a hot path, else `minor` | a collection of known small size |
| Event-loop blocking on a request path (Rule 4) | a named input size or path reaches it | `major` | startup or one-off scripts |
| Unhandled rejection (Rule 5) | per `error-handling.mdc` **Review severities** | as there | as there |
